[test-suite name=journal
  [doc [#
conformance fixtures for cx-stdlib/journal (spec/02-inprogress/xap/stdlib_journal.md
§3/§6/§10). Each program imports the bundled module via [?lib 'cx-stdlib/journal']
(resolver MUST be quoted). The LAST expression is the rendered result.

   journal is the append-only, hash-chained, tenant-partitioned event log +
   deterministic fold→state, built ON store (persistence) + hash (chain links)
   + crypto.ed25519 (snapshot signing). The four-channel model (code.md §9.1.2):
     - a committed entry is a present [entry] VALUE;
     - a failed-precondition append (stale-tail / closed / read-only / denied)
       is an [err] (failure channel);
     - an empty / out-of-range read is the ABSENCE channel — the empty
       node-set () — never null and never [err];
     - a verify / snapshot-verify of a corrupt chain is a present
       [verification valid=false …] / [snapshot-verification valid=false …]
       FINDING (a VALUE, not [err] — SAP §1).

   HERMETIC. Every case uses the mem:// backend (capability-free, deterministic)
   so fixtures need no host grant; the one file:// case is a CXER0271 denial
   (deny-lane). The default clock is a synthetic monotonic counter (ts =
   epoch:HH:MM:SS keyed off seq) so ts/hash are byte-stable across runs.

   Determinism: the entry hash is computed over the canonical CX bytes of
   seq+tenant+actor+authority+ts+prev-hash+event; genesis prev-hash is the
   fixed sentinel b3:GENESIS. The fold/replay/dry-run/snapshot/fold-from
   reducers MUST be pure (an impure $fn → CXER4611).

   Snapshot signing uses an ed25519 seed (32 bytes, hex) as opts.signing-key;
   the fixtures use the all-0x01 seed. mem:// may take an unsigned snapshot
   (opts.sign=false) usable for fold-from but NOT as a retention cover.

   Error band CXER4600–4649 (§8). Shared codes: CXER0271 (store cap denial).

   Id ranges:
     001-010  open/append/read/slice/since/head round-trip + chain link + absence
     011-018  fold / fold-slice / fold-value / replay / dry-run / determinism
     019-026  verify / verify-slice (finding-is-a-value) + tamper finding
     027-035  snapshot / snapshot-verify / fold-from (signed + unsigned + equivalence)
     036-041  retain / compact (prune-behind-snapshot + copy-forward source-intact)
     042-058  negatives / no-surface (every CXER46xx + CXER0271 denial)
   #]]

  [# ── 001-010: open / append / read / slice / since / head ───────────── #]

  [case id=journal-001-append-genesis level=core
   [tags journal append genesis chain entry]
   [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
   [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/journal']
[?let [= $j [$journal:open "mem://acme" "acme"]]
  [$journal:append $j [do :refund] {actor: "ops" authority: "d-77"}]]
#]]
   [out-text [#
[entry seq=1 tenant=acme actor=ops authority=d-77 ts='epoch:00:00:01' prev-hash=b3:GENESIS hash=sha256:bdc6c60e64d8bc43a17fc1762633a915d8816ca2dffd429b45ce19dda82d6178 [event [do :refund]]]
#]]
  ]

